{
  "schema_version": "1.9.2",
  "id": "USN-9181-1",
  "summary": "openjdk-8 vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that the JGSS component of OpenJDK 8 did not correctly\nauthenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\nor modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114939)\n\nNicholas Carlini discovered that the JSSE component of OpenJDK 8 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114940)\n\nIt was discovered that the Hotspot component of OpenJDK 8 did not correctly\nauthorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a\ndenial of service or to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114943)\n\nAlexander Dezhinov, Stanislav Dukhin, Nikita Kozlov, and Binbin Xu\ndiscovered that the Core Java Libraries component of OpenJDK 8 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114944)\n\nIt was discovered that the Compiler component of OpenJDK 8 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-114946)\n\nIn addition to security fixes, the updated packages contain bug fixes, new\nfeatures, and possibly incompatible changes.\n\nPlease see the following for more information:\nhttps://openjdk.org/groups/vulnerability/advisories/2026-11-17",
  "aliases": [],
